The user is saying "bot not initialized" when they click the TEST MEMORY HOOKS button. Looking at the code I wrote:

```csharp
private void TestMemoryHooks_Click(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)
{
    try
    {
        LogMessage("Running memory hook tests...", "INFO");
        IntPtr resultPtr = RunMemoryHookTests();

        if (resultPtr == IntPtr.Zero)
        {
            LogMessage("Test failed - no result returned", "ERROR");
            return;
        }
        ...
    }
}
```

And in BotEngine.cpp:
```cpp
const char* __cdecl RunMemoryHookTests()
{
    if (!g_botEngine || !g_botEngine->IsInitialized())
        return "Bot not initialized";
    ...
}
```

So the issue is that when the test button is clicked, the bot engine hasn't been initialized yet. The user needs to click "Initialize" first to initialize the bot engine, which creates the connection to D2R.exe and loads the memory hooks.

This is actually correct behavior - the test needs the bot to be initialized first. But I should clarify this to the user and make sure they understand they need to:

1. Click "Initialize" first
2. Then click "TEST MEMORY HOOKS"

Let me provide clear instructions.

